  "note": "Issue #145 moves the stepped trailing stop from the #139 analytics overlay into the production exit path. One pure ladder (backend/app/analytics/trailing_stop.py) is called by StrategyEvaluator.on_bar, the levels_reversal plugin (check_exit mirror + ratchet in manage_position), portfolio_backtest/portfolio_simulator and walk-forward; the bar order stop -> take -> arm and \"armed by bar i, effective from bar i+1\" are copied from #139 on purpose. The policy stays shipped OFF (TRAILING_STOP.enabled=false) and the engine fails safe: an absent key, enabled=false, an empty ladder or a ladder refused by the #144 validator does not change a single exit. The write-path gate (require_valid_trailing_stop) is still uncalled - #146 / #149 own it - and paper/live do not read the block yet (#148 / #151). Verification: 52 new unit tests, the acceptance set green, full `pytest -m \"not integration\"` suite 323 -> 375 passed with 0 new failures between origin/main and this branch, a read-only DB regression of the locked configs 126 and 36 across two git trees (regression_verdict.json), and a DB-free per-trade check against the published #143 book (grid_check.json). The backend container was not rebuilt on this machine: the stack is stopped here, so `docker compose up -d --build backend` is left to CI / the dev box.",
  "next_action": "Team Lead review + squash-merge (WORKFLOW section 8). #147 owns the formal parity gate; #146 / #149 must wire require_valid_trailing_stop() into the write paths; #148 / #151 reuse this module in paper and sandbox live."
}
